main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le08ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Clauses using <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> - Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are varying structures you can use with clauses that contain <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> forms of verbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Refer to the chart for a summary of these structures:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> -ing</span> structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verbs you use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  object +   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span> or a possessive +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span> after some verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  detest, approve, disapprove, like, dislike, hate, love, object to, forget, imagine, and remember\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">  I resented <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Sanda receiving</span> a raise.<br/> I resented <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Sandra's receiving</span> a raise.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> to</span> +   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span> after certain verbs<br/><br/>    <span class=\\\"italic\\\">to</span> + noun phrase<br/><br/>   (<span class=\\\"italic\\\">to</span> is a preposition)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" adapt, confess, object, admit, adjust, look forward, own up, and resort.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">admitted to taking</span> the last cookie. <br/><br/> They <span class=\\\"strong\\\">confessed to the crime</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Preposition +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">by</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"begin, close, end, finish (up/off), open, start\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">  Can you  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">end by saying</span> that you wish everyone a Merry Christmas?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">on</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">on</span> + object +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"concentrate, count, depend, focus, insist, rely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> My mother <span class=\\\"strong\\\">insisted on (me) wearing</span> a dress to the party.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">of</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span><br/>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"approve, hear, know, speak, talk, tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Have you ever  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">heard of (anyone you know) getting</span> arrested before? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" object +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">from</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-ing</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"deter, discourage, keep, prevent, stop, prohibit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The party next door  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">prevented me from going</span> to sleep early.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "My grandfather had a good-natured golden retriever who insisted on licking my face whenever we arrived."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I resented my brother getting a new sled."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I confessed to being a little bit jealous of my brother's gift."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My grandfather insisted on being patient."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Performative Verbs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Performative verbs are verbs which perform the action they describe. You use these verbs in the Simple Present tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples of these verbs are:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">suggest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">acknowledge </span>, <span class=\"italic\">admit, <span class=\"italic\"> advise</span>, <span class=\"italic\">apologize</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">beg</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">confess</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">congratulate</span>, <span class=\"italic\">declare</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">deny</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">forbid</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">guarantee</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">name</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">order</span>, <span class=\"italic\">permit</span> , <span class=\"italic\">predict</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">promise</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">refuse</span>, <span class=\"italic\">remind</span>, <span class=\"italic\">request</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">thank</span> and <span class=\"italic\">warn</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">suggest</span> you take the train into the city. Parking Is too expensive.<br/> They <span class=\"strong\">request</span> that we read the contract very carefully before signing.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some verbs  ( <span class=\"italic\">apologize</span>,   <span class=\"italic\">deny</span>,   <span class=\"italic\">guarantee</span>,   <span class=\"italic\">promise</span> and   <span class=\"italic\">suggest</span>) have the  same meaning in either the Simple Present to or Present Continuous forms."}, {"type": "text", "content": " For example:<br/>   <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">don't deny</span> taking the bag.</span>/|  <span class=\"italic\"> I'<span class=\"strong\">m not denying</span> taking the bag.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use modals with performative verbs to make them more polite."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">would advise</span> you not to take the bus at this time.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I must admit that I am a little bit obsessed with our furry little canine friends."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I begged my grandparents to give me one of them for Christmas."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They suggested that I wait a few more years before asking for a dog."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I acknowledge that I was more than a bit underwhelmed with my present."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I guarantee that you will not be disappointed."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I promise that you won't be disappointed. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "kindhearted "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a kind and sympathetic nature"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Like humans they can be kindhearted and personable and at times cheeky and disobedient."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about character traits."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "personable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a \u200bpleasing and \u200battractive \u200bmanner"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Like humans they can be kindhearted and personable and at times cheeky and disobedient."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cheeky"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " slightly \u200brude or \u200bshowing no \u200brespect, but often in a \u200bfunny way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Like humans they can be kindhearted and personable and at times cheeky and disobedient."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disobedient"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "refusing to obey rules or someone in authority"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Like humans they can be kindhearted and personable and at times cheeky and disobedient."}, {"type": "audio", "cont